{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'STDO|stdo-work|independent|lifecycle' /Users/jim/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"32:# Task Group: Constraint-emergence ontology and STDO methodology bridge\n34:scope: Use when applying STDO lessons to the constraint-emergence ontology; keep reality-first emergence distinct from engineering representation, assurance, and construction methods.\n35:applies_to: cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps/constraint_emergence_ontology, with comparison to /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/specification_methodology/v3; reuse_rule=safe for the conceptual distinction, consumer-relative sufficiency, and memory/data formulations; re-open the named ontology and STDO sources for any normative or current-text claim.\n37:## Task 1: Apply STDO v3 lessons to the constraint-emergence ontology, success\n45:- constraint_emergence_ontology, STDO v3, emergence on reality, memory, data, constraint topology, consumer-relative sufficiency, observation sufficiency, Markov boundary, representation, assurance\n49:- when the analysis over-focused on representation and assurance, the user corrected that the interesting aspect is “emergence on reality” -> preserve emergence of organisation, capacity and purpose-selection as the ontology’s distinctive subject; do not reduce it to STDO-style construction or assurance. [Task 1]\n56:- STDO transfers most directly through consumer-relative sufficiency: if a representation maps two cases to the same observation while their required decisions differ, it has discarded a material distinction. This is not by itself a Markov-boundary proof or a general compression theorem. [Task 1]\n57:- The ontology’s recursive emergence account is: interactions produce persistent organisation; organisation changes the conditions of later interactions; those altered conditions enable further organisation. STDO is a bounded engineering instance within this broader reality-first account. [Task 1]\n61:- symptom: synthesis becomes an STDO representation/assurance account -> cause: its engineering machinery displaced the ontology’s actual subject -> fix: lead with emergence, persistence, memory, and changing transformation topology; then import STDO distinctions as bounded engineering cases. [Task 1]\n62:- symptom: iteration, convergence, or persistence is called reliability or emergent organisation -> cause: agreement/shared error and ordinary statefulness were conflated with emergence -> fix: preserve uncertainty, non-performance, and failed evidence; require independently defined formation, boundary, persistence, and dynamics for an emergence claim. [Task 1]\n64:# Task Group: ABIogenesis GTL/ABG/STDO formal-model strategy review\n66:scope: Use for read-only review of formal GTL/ABG/STDO cases about representation, retention, qualification, and continuation-sensitive preservation.\n67:applies_to: cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps/abiogenesis, with STDO v3 comparison; reuse_rule=safe for the review method and claim boundaries; the reviewed strategy path, hashes, and no-blocking disposition are specific to the 2026-10-24 cut.\n69:## Task 1: Review rewritten GTL/ABG/STDO formal model, success\n77:- GTL, ABG, STDO, formal model, candidate-only projection, qualified view, continuation-sensitive preservation, complete presentation environment, retained terms, fixed-Γ, typed annotations\n89:# Task Group: STDO v3.0.1 F_D widening and migration proposal review\n91:scope: Use when reviewing a proposed STDO v3.0.1 widening of F_D, legacy-operation migration, or exhaustion semantics; preserve authority and proposal-status boundaries.\n94:## Task 1: Review and re-read STDO 3.0.1 change proposal, success\n102:- STDO 3.0.1, F_D, deterministic processing, ODD authority migration, totality, closed dependencies, exhaustion, candidate availability, indeterminate, residual work, stdo verify\n220:- T-287 remains design-accepted but implementation, affected proof, L5 acceptance, and release resumption are open. Resolve lifecycle/failure handoff and six value-owner obligations plus two native composite classifications; implement mechanics and consumer adoption; freeze one combined candidate; run isolated build/type/focused proof; execute installed P1-P5 proof; then independently assess L5. Stop at the first genuine integration failure and return its causal boundary to Executive triage. [Task 1]\n221:- The proposed proof order was P1 installed Public setup without native actor, then P2/P3/P5 prerequisites, and P4 one native STDO3 execution only after earlier gates. Estimates (15–30 elapsed hours / 2–4 working days) were uncertain, especially truthful producer types, resource-vs-data boundaries, and schema ingress. [Task 1]\n227:- symptom: broad repeated reviews create churn -> cause: Executive/reviewer contexts and grant boundaries blur -> fix: keep reviewers independent and escalate only a named unresolved design/authority question while preserving accepted evidence. [Task 1]\n247:- Grantland's follow-up reported generally net-positive reactions among contacted businesses and a reported roughly 10% sales bump for Valley's Pizza Land. Vulture/New York Magazine and Grantland are stronger evidence than Reddit anecdotes; distinguish independently reported interviews from participant-attributed accounts. [Task 1]\n270:- when the user says “dude just give me some locations in sydney do what you can” and then “no i want lenovo at this point” -> give concrete manufacturer-specific options first; clearly separate verified authorised locations from alternatives and do not substitute independent repairers. [Task 1]\n281:- symptom: generic caution or independent repairers displace the requested Lenovo route -> cause: provider preference was not recognized early -> fix: lead with manufacturer/authorised routing and label alternatives separately. [Task 1]\n351:- when reviewing work called “complete” or `candidate_ready` -> preserve candidate construction, independent evidence, owner acceptance, integrated qualification, publication, and release as separate states. [Task 1]\n365:# Task Group: STDO v3 I3 common-contract review\n367:scope: Use for frozen I3 cross-review or qualification-status reporting; keep mechanical coherence, semantic fidelity, practical evidence, independent review, owner acceptance, and release separate.\n378:- STDO v3, I3, Codex, frozen-source-review, `7c058ed52b9f3cdecf6277026be5d18507efc527`, `d832a51a4f91afca2ffa2e31636236f8729abf6c`, artifact-checker, stale derived artifacts, frontier pins, successor-conservation, result-algebra, independent-review\n388:- The installed predecessor verification passed; all 30 consolidated input hashes matched. The frozen common subject was `7c058ed52b9f3cdecf6277026be5d18507efc527`; Codex checkpoint `d832a51a4f91afca2ffa2e31636236f8729abf6c`. Keep the sequence source coverage/repair -> dispositions and derived artifacts -> coherent freeze -> practical tests -> independent review -> owner acceptance/release. [Task 1]\n392:- symptom: the frozen checker reports 736 failures -> cause: inventories, conservation pins, frame excerpts, and compression pins bind earlier source -> fix: treat 16 inventory, 599 frontier, 95 excerpt, and 26 compression failures as stale-derived-artifact incoherence, not independent semantic defects; do not refresh hashes and call the candidate correct. [Task 1]\n411:- when repairs follow independent review, preserve separate Executive/Worker/Reviewer authority and use exact write territory, closed evidence, and independent review before further edits; avoid broad churn. [Task 1]\n417:- Integration-003's 273 tests/no skips, 9-file strict typing, 9 upstream checks, and 10 CLI/MCP checks are historical pre-repair evidence. The worker later reported 35 focused tests and 5-file typing, but sealed evidence, independent delta review, and final integration were absent. [Task 1]\n421:- symptom: a green archived integration is cited as repair closure -> cause: the test count belongs to the pre-repair cut -> fix: require a new frozen source, focused checks, sealed implementation evidence, independent delta review, and final integration. [Task 1]\n478:- rollout_summaries/2026-09-29T15-14-42-7gWO-abiogenesis_consumer_reuse_repair_accepted_rc1_open.md (cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/09/30/rollout-2026-09-30T01-14-42-01a0edbb-7c4f-7493-bf06-2a600644bbb6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-05T02:00:55+00:00, thread_id=01a0edbb-7c4f-7493-bf06-2a600644bbb6, independently accepted bounded consumer-preparation/recovery cut)\n496:- when resuming this work, the user required reading the durable handoff, preserving the dirty worktree and accepted evidence, and not repeating completed investigations -> start from the named handoff/checkpoint; do not reset, clean, broadly rescan, or rerun lifecycle work without need. [Task 1]\n497:- when a bounded run hit an integration/oracle mismatch -> stop at the first failure, preserve the failed cut, correct only the owning caller/test, and obtain independent review rather than blindly retrying or changing the framework. [Task 2]\n502:- Authority order is `GOALS.md` -> `INTENT.md` -> `PRODUCT.md` -> requirements -> accepted design -> active ticket. Comments, generated views, and tests are evidence, not Product authority. Executive coordinates/disposition only; source mutation needs explicit Writer/Worker activation and independent review of a frozen result. [Task 1]\n516:scope: Use for bounded `odd_manager` integration with a frozen ABIogenesis 5 observation contract, independent qualification of the Run Inspector slice, or a requested full-worktree checkpoint/push.\n517:applies_to: cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps/odd_manager (rollout launched from /Users/jim/src/apps); reuse_rule=safe for the ownership boundary, contract-validation shields, and requested-checkpoint workflow; treat STDO/profile/candidate digests, file counts, commit, and remote state as time-specific to the 2026-09-29 rollout.\n527:- odd_manager, ABIogenesis 5, ABG5, RC1, T-046, I-01, Run Inspector, event-stream, STDO v2.5.1-rc.1, causal-reference, run-replay, ddc961, active, gap_stopped, abg-event-carrier-service.mjs\n546:- I-01/T-046 was accepted only for the frozen `sha256:ddc961a2484be150193fa255d7dc7b933e52fb81b7b2c681f2bb97e1f9d5754c` event profile/base Run replay branch under STDO `v2.5.1-rc.1`, manifest `5d306da13994e69aa9f215d4c1cd2d0be96283c1e33a652b58e6e9262d036b64`; later upstream changes need a new delta and qualification. [Task 1]\n549:- For an authorized full checkpoint, `git diff --check`, stage the explicitly requested whole visible tree, push, then independently compare `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/main` with `HEAD` and use `git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...origin/main`; see `skills/full-worktree-checkpoint/SKILL.md`. [Task 2]\n557:# Task Group: Trade Calculus modular performance and independent-assurance specification\n559:scope: Use when changing or reviewing the Trade Calculus specification for performance-critical, selectively isolated, semantically composable trading components and their independent assurance.\n570:- trade_calculus, MODULAR_TRADING_FRAMEWORK.md, modular-trading-framework, trading performance, selective isolation, plug and play, independent assurance, semantic component contracts, REQ-28, REQ-33, S-29, S-34, /definition/modular-framework, T-007\n574:- when the user clarified that “trading performance is critical” while the framework allows “selective isolation” and a “plug and play system” -> preserve commercial-performance goals alongside modular, independently verifiable components. [Task 1]\n580:- Keep four findings independent: implementation/semantic conformance, empirical model adequacy, trading performance, and governance eligibility. A profitable result does not prove conformance or permission; conformance does not prove predictive edge. [Task 1]\n582:- `REQ-28`–`REQ-33` and falsifiers `S-29`–`S-34` are open framework obligations. The PoC reports bounded economic results and must not claim commercial edge, full component admission/substitution, complete external execution lifecycle, persistent assurance records, or independent regulatory verification. [Task 1]\n592:applies_to: cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps/abiogenesis (rollout launched from /Users/jim/src/apps); reuse_rule=safe for review scope discovery, authority order, and frozen-subject discipline; treat HEAD, remote state, worktree counts, STDO basis, and exact work records as time-specific to the 2026-09-29 review.\n623:# Task Group: STDO strategy commentary and ABIogenesis-local law placement\n625:scope: Use when turning ABIogenesis architecture findings into a non-authoritative STDO strategy post that separates reusable method recommendations from project Product/design/requirements/local axioms.\n626:applies_to: cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/specification_methodology; reuse_rule=safe for authority-owner classification and commentary-only workflow; treat the selected STDO release, manifest, post contents, and validation counts as time-specific to the 2026-09-20 rollout.\n628:## Task 1: Publish provisional STDO revision recommendations plus project-local law placement, success\n632:- rollout_summaries/2026-07-31T04-44-25-WpNO-abiogenesis_status_code_review_and_stdo_strategy.md (cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/07/31/rollout-2026-07-31T14-44-25-019fb67c-e134-7de0-9b85-7dbcfaf5a164.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-20T04:55:22+00:00, thread_id=019fb67c-e134-7de0-9b85-7dbcfaf5a164, uncommitted strategy post with shared STDO and ABIogenesis-local recommendations)\n636:- STDO, strategy-post, local-axioms, stdo://releases/v2.5.0-rc.4/, 4fa2556d, T-288, ABI5_REALIZATION_CONSTITUTION.md, Q1-Q7, .ai-workspace/comments/codex/20260920T044837Z_STRATEGY_stdo_251_postmortem_consolidation_and_project_local_law.md\n640:- when the user asked to “post your findings as strategy with detailed recommendations to STDO revision” and said some findings “may better be within the local axioms of a project” -> explicitly classify each recommendation by authority owner: shared STDO amendment, project Product/requirements, local axioms/reference-frame bindings, or implementation fix. [Task 1]\n645:- STDO owns reusable validity, review, qualification, compression-fidelity, and evidence relations; ABIogenesis owns runtime events, Event Calculus/replay, worksite observations, concrete counters, threat model, and implementation mechanisms. Do not turn shared recommendations into universal runtime architecture. [Task 1]\n646:- The created commentary post is `.ai-workspace/comments/codex/20260920T044837Z_STRATEGY_stdo_251_postmortem_consolidation_and_project_local_law.md`; it contains eight shared STDO recommendations, eight ABIogenesis-local recommendations, Q1-Q7 qualification cases, and ownership tables. [Task 1]\n695:- symptom: a full code-level findings report is needed after Gate 1 -> cause: the rollout pivoted to STDO before completing that report -> fix: treat this review as incomplete and re-open live code from `root_operation_state.ts`, `public/operations.ts`, and the durable projection carriers. [Task 2]\n701:scope: Use after an authorized ABIogenesis recovery from a rejected development cut, when restoring only selected archived commentary, or when locating the restored four-dimensional lifecycle post.\n724:## Task 3: Locate the restored four-dimensional lifecycle post, success\n732:- Living Product Lifecycle In An N-Dimensional Workspace, .ai-workspace/comments/codex, 20260822T034200Z_STRATEGY_living_four_dimensional_product_lifecycle.md, VS Code Quick Open, hidden dot-directory, current main\n739:- when looking for the lifecycle post in VS Code -> provide the repository-relative path and explain that `.ai-workspace` is a hidden dot-directory. [Task 3]\n746:- `Living Product Lifecycle In An N-Dimensional Workspace` is a tracked file on current `main` at `.ai-workspace/comments/codex/20260822T034200Z_STRATEGY_living_four_dimensional_product_lifecycle.md`, not a branch folder. Its operational cut is composition/identity, authority/meaning, causal time, and homeostatic control. [Task 3]\n777:# Task Group: abiogenesis lifecycle strategy commentary, practical architecture, and authority-flow amendment\n787:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-22T03-16-39-vV9C-abiogenesis_strategic_lifecycle_post_review.md (cwd=/Users/jim/Documents/Codex/2026-08-22/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/22/rollout-2026-08-22T13-16-39-01a02778-6e79-7462-a7e7-7c17ffde1860.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-24T11:25:11+00:00, thread_id=01a02778-6e79-7462-a7e7-7c17ffde1860, authoritative-checkout orientation and catalog/Consensus authority model)\n793:## Task 2: Create a Mermaid-rich lifecycle strategy post and verify its GitHub visibility, partial\n797:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-22T03-36-35-y4oK-abiogenesis_lifecycle_strategy_post_local_commit_github_link.md (cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/22/rollout-2026-08-22T13-36-35-01a0278a-b028-7361-8928-230a7680bf5e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-22T04:12:10+00:00, thread_id=01a0278a-b028-7361-8928-230a7680bf5e, post committed locally; remote visibility and working-tree parity were not established)\n801:- strategy-post, Mermaid, mmdc, POSTING_GUIDE.md, GraphFunction, Consensus, homeostatic-lifecycle, 35eff784, origin/main, local-only, dirty-worktree, GitHub link\n803:## Task 3: Independently review the committed living-lifecycle strategy, success\n807:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-22T03-58-56-YLgD-abiogenesis_living_lifecycle_strategy_review.md (cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/22/rollout-2026-08-22T13-58-56-01a0279f-2786-7801-96b4-85c4ca8d5e33.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-22T04:11:10+00:00, thread_id=01a0279f-2786-7801-96b4-85c4ca8d5e33, review-only; CHANGES REQUESTED on four material issues)\n811:- living-lifecycle, Consensus, One Surface, ConstructionIntent, ActionCatalog, evaluateNext, evaluateAction, replay, Mermaid, STDO, REQ-P-CONSENSUS-010, REQ-P-CONSENSUS-012, T-270\n813:## Task 4: Amend and commit only the named lifecycle commentary post, success\n817:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-22T04-02-16-RuKG-abiogenesis_n_dimensional_lifecycle_strategy_post.md (cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/22/rollout-2026-08-22T14-02-16-01a027a2-331f-7b60-a1db-1511d341a20e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-22T04:18:28+00:00, thread_id=01a027a2-331f-7b60-a1db-1511d341a20e, named-path revision/validation/commit in a dirty worktree)\n818:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-22T03-16-39-vV9C-abiogenesis_strategic_lifecycle_post_review.md (cwd=/Users/jim/Documents/Codex/2026-08-22/realtime-voice-chat, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/22/rollout-2026-08-22T13-16-39-01a02778-6e79-7462-a7e7-7c17ffde1860.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-24T11:25:11+00:00, thread_id=01a02778-6e79-7462-a7e7-7c17ffde1860, strategic-post correction and final named-post commit)\n822:- .ai-workspace/comments/codex/20260822T034200Z_STRATEGY_living_four_dimensional_product_lifecycle.md, strategy-post, manifold, reference-frame, intent-vector, gain-function, Product catalog, admitted Program, ActionCatalog, evaluateNext, Product-parameter gate, Consensus, Pandoc, git diff --check, 683f3ea8\n828:- when an independent pass is requested as “Do not edit files, amend commits, or change repository state” -> keep the review read-only and lead with concrete severity-ranked findings. [Task 3]\n829:- when the user requested an executive foreword plus Mermaid lifecycle and entity/domain diagrams -> provide focused visual explanations, then independently review semantic authority/admission meaning as well as syntax/rendering. [Task 2][Task 3][Task 4]\n835:- In the designated checkout, ABG5-S05 under T-270 is the current selector and S03 is accepted. “Wave 2” does not occur literally, so any mapping to S05 is an inference; S05 remains short of full closure because independent exact-cut review is pending. [Task 1]\n844:- symptom: a lifecycle diagram is syntactically valid but shows Consensus before its own admission, gives `DISPOSITION -> GOVERNED_INTENT -> ADMITTED_INVOCATION`, or omits `evaluateAction`/closure/refresh -> cause: catalog, selection, admission, and authority layers were collapsed -> fix: semantically review optionality, authority, admission order, and re-entry; draw Consensus as an ordinary nested invocation and preserve typed no-action, F_H, ticket/reprice, refusal, and re-entry outcomes. [Task 3][Task 4]\n848:# Task Group: specification_methodology STDO constitutional and Product Definition overlay reviews\n850:scope: Use for substantive STDO/DMM constitutional-amendment review, exact candidate qualification/release gating, and review-only analysis of the Product Definition overlay in `specification_methodology`.\n853:## Task 1: Review STDO Product Definition Overlay, uncertain\n861:- STDO, Product Definition Overlay, SPEC_METHOD.md, stdo_<label>.json, constitution.authorities, how.build_tenants, product-definition.schema.json, PRODUCT_DEFINITION_TEMPLATE.json, Draft 2020-12, JSON Schema format, compression digest\n871:- STDO, T-005, SPEC_METHOD, DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD, transformation admission, projection non-authority, Prime mapping, recurrence/commonization, C5, per-source-function tracing, convergence\n877:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-02T04-34-55-m4X7-stdo_t005_t008_substantive_review_rc2_preparation.md (cwd=/Users/jim, rollout_path=/Users/jim/.codex/sessions/2026/08/02/rollout-2026-08-02T14-34-55-019fc0c0-e8e5-7fb0-a7bf-e3af3b52b7e1.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T15:46:32+00:00, thread_id=019fc0c0-e8e5-7fb0-a7bf-e3af3b52b7e1, Candidate 03 and RC2 passed independent semantic/exact-cut review; final release publication remained pending direct user acceptance)\n886:- when the review focused on ticket mechanics, the user said: “put aside paperwork, i want a meaningful review of content ... understand STDO, and understand the ticket amendments, ignore procedural for a second” -> lead with substantive law, duplication, scope, and semantic-gap analysis; treat process metadata as secondary [Task 2]\n892:- The overlay is a layout-neutral locator/relation map, not a rival authority surface: one `stdo_<label>.json` per distinct WHAT; URI bindings are layout-independent; `how.build_tenants` holds one or more canonical tenant identities/locations; composition is explicit and recursive discovery creates no implicit inheritance. Referenced WHAT, HOW, ticket, and commentary documents retain their own meaning. [Task 1]\n893:- `constitution.authorities` must identify a complete immutable STDO cut; entrypoints are navigation only. Schema validity does not prove URI resolution, release identity, cross-definition uniqueness, constitutional sufficiency, or authority congruence. [Task 1]\n895:- T-005 had a legitimate kernel: DMM role matrices can leave ambiguous which complete admission relation turns a candidate entity transformation into durable truth. Close that gap narrowly; existing STDO already covers material relation sets, lifecycle and authority matrices, projection non-authority, Prime mapping, and recurrence/commonization. [Task 2]\n898:- Candidate 03 passed two clean independent semantic reviews. RC2 commit/tree were `e204f3bb287651daedefa9ea28f1c2c7cc387787` / `908373dabadc75cdf5327d05b0448aedac83f502`; tag `v2.3.1-rc.2` (object `e76a4988066834860b1ae988e1ffa84ef31219f7`) was published atomically to `main`, `rc/2.3.1`, and the tag; RC1 was unchanged. Two independent exact-cut reviews found no issues and the final-delta proof was zero for Product/release-scoped bytes. [Task 3]\n1002:scope: Use for Sydney CBD cake-specific recommendations or current-launch accessory research; distinguish venue/product claims from independently verified availability, fit, and quality.\n1067:- when the user says they prefer “2 split units” -> prioritize two twin-head systems over ducted or four-independent options, while treating sizing as a provisional quote brief. [Task 1]\n1073:- A 2.5 kW plus 3.5 kW indoor pairing can connect to one multi-split outdoor unit; two twin-head reverse-cycle systems are a feasible four-bedroom plan. Heads have independent room controls, but heads sharing an outdoor unit generally must use the same heating/cooling mode. [Task 1]\n1081:- symptom: nearby installer credentials are presented as quality proof -> cause: published capability/location was confused with independently verified workmanship/current availability -> fix: label the shortlist as published-service-based and seek site assessment and written quote. [Task 2]\n1083:# Task Group: STDO v3 Claude/Codex tenant comparison criteria and categorical review protocol\n1085:scope: Use for independent STDO v3 tenant review and non-authoritative commentary criteria; protect peer isolation, common authority, semantic assessment, and bounded evaluation decisions.\n1086:applies_to: cwd=/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/specification_methodology/v3 (earlier C1 layout also used /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology/stdo_3); reuse_rule=re-baseline from the live Product Definition and installed STDO before reuse; treat candidate paths, commits, hashes, criteria-post status, and proposed budget as time-specific.\n1096:- STDO v3, C1, Claude, Codex, independent implementations, freeze, peer isolation, common pen, stdo status --definition stdo_3/stdo_3.json --verify, F_D, F_P, F_H\n1110:- when work is framed as “two independent implementations” with cross-review only after both returns freeze -> preserve peer isolation, freeze exact subjects first, and never let a tenant review repair or accept its own candidate. [Task 1]\n1113:- when the user identifies themselves as a comparison subject -> disclose authorship and tenant-family conflicts; an author cannot independently establish acceptance of their own work. [Task 2]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
