cit and verifies the identity it expects. | [§1](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#1-overlay-and-layout-independence), the identity paragraphs; [§9](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#9-recursive-discovery-and-explicit-composition) | the composition entry fields and the checks of a conforming discovered set: domain choices of this member | 1, 2 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/frames/bootstrap.md:1027:### Foundation to law\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/frames/bootstrap.md:1064:| P0 (recovered), P5 (derived from P0 and P6, with P0's open-world premise), P6 (independent); instance premise a | By P0 an actor's envelope is finite, and by P5 a step cannot report success on what it did not hold, so frame adequacy includes actor usability. When the material manifold exceeds an actor's envelope, the lawful responses are another actor, a refined frame or outer contract, sequenced activations, a lawful compression or `out_of_frame`; silently omitting material relations to fit is never one of them, and a frame never silently grows beyond the selected actor's envelope. Actor capability may justify a different frame size or activation sequence, and can neither waive an invariant nor widen authority | [RF-014](../REFERENCE_FRAME.md#rf-014-capability-fit); [ACTIVATION §2](../ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope) step 3, the responses when the context does not fit, outside this member; [FOUNDATIONS §2 Frame objects](../FOUNDATIONS.md#frame-objects), Capability envelope, outside this member; [§11](../REFERENCE_FRAME.md#11-the-activation-packet), frame size; [§12](../REFERENCE_FRAME.md#12-violations) item 10 | the selection among these responses: human authority, directly or in advance through the grant; which responses a step selects within its grant (refinement, sequencing, compression) and which re-enter the owner of the grant or envelope (another actor, a larger envelope): ACTIVATION §2 step 3 | 7, 8 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/frames/bootstrap.md:1066:| P0 (recovered, with its actor-change premise), P3 (independent), P6 (independent); instance premise e | By P0's actor-change premise and P3 an input is acquired by exact identity from the selected basis, and by P6 absence from view grants nothing, so declared inputs are acquired by exact identity, and only from the exact selected basis: a declared input absent from the actor's view is neither licence to read elsewhere nor evidence that it is absent, and a candidate source, a moving selector or another basis is no substitute. Where a derived surface is stale, missing or insufficient for a named question, the deciding owner sections are acquired directly. Acquisition is read-only, grants no role, operation or decision, and a missing binding is returned with its outcome before any dependent action | [ACTIVATION §2](../ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope) step 4 and Acquisition, outside this member | acquiring a current derived surface in preference to its owning sections where it serves the task: ACTIVATION §2 Acquisition; which derived surfaces are published: their publisher, and none owns a determination | 2, 7 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/frames/bootstrap.md:1087:### Foundation to law: chain, outcome and build-tenant binding\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1:# ACTIVATION\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:27:## 1. The step\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:69:| P5 (derived from P0 and P6, with P0's open-world premise), P2 (independent), P6 (independent); instance premise d | By P5 a non-satisfied result leaves the outcome undecided or failed, by P2 work continues only toward the outcome, and by P6 a hard stop is no policy decision, so every non-satisfied result has a named next move, an explicit unknown class included, and reconfiguration follows the cause; a hard stop holds whatever the risk appetite | [§4](#4-totality-and-refinement), Hard stops and the paragraphs before Refinement | the ambiguity policy and its risk appetite: the project's declared policy ([SPEC_METHOD §5](SPEC_METHOD.md#5-ambiguity-governance-and-lifecycle)) | 5 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:104:- Row 7, totality and hard stops: [EVALUATION §5 When a finding blocks promotion](EVALUATION.md#when-a-finding-blocks-promotion); [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE Technical triage](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#technical-triage-severity-priority-and-boundary-effect); [SPEC_METHOD §5](SPEC_METHOD.md#5-ambiguity-governance-and-lifecycle); [DESIGN_MODULE Post-ticket design review](DESIGN_MODULE.md#post-ticket-design-review); the [WORLD_MODEL family table](WORLD_MODEL.md#foundation-to-law).\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:116:### Transitions\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:177:ambiguity that halts the work or exceeds the step's authority stops it\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:199:### Construction relation\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:353:### Intake\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:391:### Execution unit\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:402:### Admission\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:439:### Applicability\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:445:obligation, under its cited authority; a missing or ambiguous premise\n/Users/jim/Lib