d | policy permits work to continue with the ambiguity open; the open ambiguity is the counterexample, and it stays a recorded residual that names the evidence or decision that would resolve it |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1101:| `blocked` | falsified | the ambiguity stays unresolved, and policy or a hard stop (§4) halts work at it; the open ambiguity is the counterexample, and the value names the halting condition and what would lift it |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1103:An open ambiguity is a known state of the exact basis, so `carried` and\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1106:the value: `carried` with what would resolve the ambiguity, `blocked` with\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1109:dependent claim cannot rest on a carried, escalated or blocked ambiguity\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1110:as if it were resolved. The mapping places ambiguity outcomes\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1114:### Effects\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1164:## 4. Totality and refinement\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1183:Which outcome of [§3 Ambiguity outcome](#ambiguity-outcome) a declared\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1184:ambiguity takes is decided by the applicable ambiguity policy and its risk\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1186:policy is [SPEC_METHOD §5](SPEC_METHOD.md#5-ambiguity-governance-and-lifecycle),\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1189:Hard stops. Some conditions are not optional ambiguity decisions and\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1195:for a declared ambiguity, with the §3 Ambiguity outcome `blocked`;\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1198:[SPEC_METHOD §5](SPEC_METHOD.md#5-ambiguity-governance-and-lifecycle)\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1210:### Refinement\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1286:### Complete enclosing-relation admission\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1300:production and invalidation are recoverable; an unsupported assertion of\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1338:### Standing structural qualification\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1350:| direct | the complete direct relation is derived, validated and admitted once |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1351:| supported composite or nested | every supported constituent and owning boundary satisfies the same law; unsupported forms have a design-grounded `not_applicable` disposition and no weaker or competing path |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1353:| ambiguous enclosing relation | unresolved participant, join, seam or relation identity ambiguity is refused without effect |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1370:## 5. Work state and restart\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1458:### The workspace and an actor's account\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1519:## 6. Cost and proportionality\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1521:Proportionality is the relation between semantic ambiguity removed and\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1538:realisation space. Each constraint identifies the semantic ambiguity it\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1565:surface without materially reducing ambiguity; existing obligations should\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1606:| P2 (independent), P0 (recovered); instance premise b | By P2 an obligation is justified only by its route to the outcome, and by P0 reasoning capacity is finite, so a method obligation is proportional only when the ambiguity it removes justifies the reasoning complexity it adds, and that complexity is not raw size | [§6](#6-cost-and-proportionality), first three paragraphs | the justification of a constraint family: its owning law, once for the family | 6, 7 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1607:| P2 (independent), P0 (recovered), P1 (independent); instance premise b | By P2 and P0 detail is justified where it resolves alternatives the actor can hold, and by P1 a duplicate of truth is a second representation, not more truth, so a detailed symbolic design that resolves material alternatives within reasoning capacity is proportional; an addition that duplicates truth or adds reconciliation paths without reducing ambiguity is not | [§6](#6-cost-and-proportionality), symbolic-design paragraph | none | 4, 6 |\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1617:- Row 1, the proportionality relation: [§1 Configuration](#configuration), whose explanation of an allocation is proportional, and [Roles and delegation](#roles-and-delegation), where a review or ceremony that no law requires adds reasoning cost without removing ambiguity; [§7 Transition evidence](#transition-evidence), whose proof cadence uses the cheapest focused proof unless the affected risk makes whole-candidate proof necessary; [DESIGN_MODULE §5](DESIGN_MODULE.md#5-ontology-first-design), its opening, and [Proportional design sequencing](DESIGN_MODULE.md#proportional-design-sequencing), where the relation selects between co-evolution and a design gate; [§6 Boundary and governance cost (UP-005)](DESIGN_MODULE.md#boundary-and-governance-cost-up-005), which applies the relation to Prime contraction; [Capability and foundation selection (UP-023)](DESIGN_MODULE.md#capability-and-foundation-selection-up-023), whose selection pass is applied proportionally; [CONFORMANCE §1](CONFORMANCE.md#1-counterexample-cases), case C-12, and [§5](CONFORMANCE.md#5-discriminator-coverage), discriminator 41.\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1627:### Resource limits\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1681:## 7. Closed result and reuse\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1712:results. Invalidation withdraws the result from direct reliance; whether\n/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/ACTIVATION.md:1750:### Transition evidence\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"The checks found three separate blockers: Alpha’s specified store lacks the pinned release, Beta’s installed release has a changed standards file, and Gamma has no Product selection. Native `results.conjoin` discovery refused the capability, and the build failed because `inputs/dependency.txt` is missing. I’ll record those results and leave the greetings and built-output placeholder unchanged.\n"}}
