{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-lifecycle-m2ap70vo/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 a4fd7326ebd923db0523e22b8ca2fd82bcb80fed2e0d870c83407d69c94da7cf --principal host call --request - <<'STDO_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"diagnostics-source-method-1-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"95afb85e4cf8f248a6f430be34ef288add61445dc43d9c8121239409b9fac231\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[225,320]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nSTDO_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:08a95d535f26799d707144ac17c196e7db1ae34d5fb164d1531ba519ac1f0b62\",\"sha256\":\"08a95d535f26799d707144ac17c196e7db1ae34d5fb164d1531ba519ac1f0b62\"},\"id\":\"diagnostics-source-method-1-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=7d9131d78961a1f9898b8edb7e7594c904def7ede79423b43c088cd53e57797d]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 4. Shared installed release basis and toolchain manager\\n\\nWithin the product-definition-routing context an Installed Release Basis\\nis the pair (P3):\\n\\n```text\\n(immutable stdo://releases/<cut>/ URI, installed-manifest SHA-256)\\n```\\n\\nThe URI identifies one immutable annotated RC cut. The digest identifies\\nthe deterministic installed-release manifest, which binds the cut's tag\\nobject, commit, repository tree, standards subtree, exact standards\\ninventory, member bytes and admitted auxiliary payloads. The manifest shape\\nis owned by `schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json`. The manifest\\nis transport and integrity evidence, not a replacement constitution (P6).\\n\\nAn Adoption Plan is the read-only, deterministic acceptance object that\\nbinds one current Product Definition's identity and bytes to its current\\nbasis and to one resolved immutable target's cut, annotated tag object,\\ncommit, tree and installed-manifest digest. Its SHA-256 is the\\noperator-presentable acceptance token. Possession of the token alone grants\\nno authority; a mismatch proves that the presented subject is no longer the\\nsubject being mutated (P6, P3). A Fleet Adoption Plan binds an authorised\\nfleet root and the complete ordered set of per-definition plan digests\\nunder the same law.\\n\\nPlan hashing covers the acceptance object only: local installation status\\nand machine-local install paths are excluded. The canonical bytes are UTF-8\\nJSON with recursively sorted object keys, two-space indentation, LF line\\nendings and one final LF. Fleet order is deterministic discovery-path\\norder. These rules make a presented digest independently reproducible\\nrather than an opaque session token (P3, P6).\\n\\nThe STDO Toolchain Manager is the bounded executable realisation that (P2,\\nP3):\\n\\n- installs each immutable cut once in a shared, versioned release store;\\n- resolves logical `stdo://releases/...` URIs to verified installed bytes;\\n- inventories and verifies complete installed distributions;\\n- synchronises the exact basis already selected by a Product Definition;\\n- emits an exact digest-bound adoption plan from a mutable version-line\\n  selector and performs adoption only when that plan is explicitly\\n  accepted;\\n- manages the stable marker-bounded bootstrap in declared agent files; and\\n- applies those operations to an explicitly discovered fleet of Product\\n  Definitions.\\n\\nThe store may live at any machine-local path. Its registry maps logical\\nrelease URIs to installed paths and manifest digests and owns neither\\nProduct selection nor method meaning. A consumer repository therefore needs\\nno project-local standards copy and no prescribed folder structure, and\\nseveral Product Definitions on one machine may select different installed\\ncuts concurrently (P3, P6). Every manager-owned component from the\\nconfigured store root downward is a physical directory or regular file of\\nits declared type; a symlink, junction, reparse point, device, socket or\\nother redirection or special entry fails closed. Verification inventories\\nevery filesystem entry type, directories included, rejects any entry not\\nderived from the manifest's exact file paths, and never follows an\\nunmanifested alias (P5, P3).\\n\\n`constitution.stdo.source.repository` identifies the transport source.\\n`constitution.stdo.selector` is a mutable `stdo://channels/<version>`\\ndiscovery selector whose alias semantics are owned by the release law (the\\n[RELEASE](RELEASE.md) member). Neither is operative authority.\\n`constitution.stdo.basis.uri` and `constitution.stdo.basis.manifest_sha256`\\nare the sole authored STDO selection for that Product Definition (P6, P3).\\n\\nThe manager observes these command boundaries (P6, P5):\\n\\n- `install` admits one explicitly named immutable RC cut without changing\\n  any Product Definition;\\n- `sync` installs and verifies only the exact basis already selected by\\n  the Product Definition and never consults its mutable selector;\\n- `adopt --dry-run` resolves the annotated selector and immutable RC, and\\n  presents the target cut, tag object, commit, tree, manifest digest,\\n  current Product-Definition byte digest and a deterministic\\n  adoption-plan digest, without mutation;\\n- mutating `adopt` requires that exact prior plan digest as explicit\\n  acceptance, re-derives it before installation, installs only the bound\\n  target, rechecks the Product Definition bytes, and atomically changes\\n  only its basis and its basis-relative schema locator; any drift refuses\\n  mutation;\\n- `status`, `verify`, `list`, `manifest` and `resolve` are read-only with\\n  respect to Product Definitions; and\\n- fleet adoption emits, and requires explicit acceptance of, one aggregate\\n  plan digest over every per-definition plan; all fleet writes require\\n  explicit whole-selection authorisation and infer no composition or\\n  inheritance from directory nesting.\\n\\nMissing cuts, moved immutable tags, tag-to-commit mismatch, manifest-digest\\nmismatch, missing, extra or changed installed members, ambiguous Product\\nDefinition discovery, unaccepted or stale adoption plans, URI escape,\\nphysical store redirection, undeclared filesystem entry types and malformed\\nbootstrap markers fail closed (P5). Every `stdo:` schema locator is parsed\\nbefore schema loading under URI scheme case-insensitivity and names the\\nsame immutable cut as `constitution.stdo.basis`; spelling variation cannot\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[225,320]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"95afb85e4cf8f248a6f430be34ef288add61445dc43d9c8121239409b9fac231\",\"selected_sha256\":\"3fd4477d814964d8760ec722e2a081a5c1e75770af5d51561a6314bf121137f2\",\"size_bytes\":5334,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[225,320]},\"sha256\":\"95afb85e4cf8f248a6f430be34ef288add61445dc43d9c8121239409b9fac231\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-lifecycle-m2ap70vo/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 a4fd7326ebd923db0523e22b8ca2fd82bcb80fed2e0d870c83407d69c94da7cf --principal host call --request - <<'STDO_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"diagnostics-source-method-0-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/frames/bootstrap.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"cbf4a10e8d0b4ca2ab4a1f3ee28a85ffedc3298a0fba666949d9b091e82cc714\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1,160]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nSTDO_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:281b49fe8128f727afd10ee961be6a99e00bc7fbcf5109b0d7f965fd07c2462d\",\"sha256\":\"281b49fe8128f727afd10ee961be6a99e00bc7fbcf5109b0d7f965fd07c2462d\"},\"id\":\"diagnostics-source-method-0-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=3225eb6060947b7a74f170689b3224ffbbd582764929e29003d17a44dce458ee]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Reference frame bootstrap\\n\\nTask: Enter this method for a task not yet specified: say what the method is, bind the exact basis and the one applicable product definition, say how a reference frame is activated for a step and what the step may and may not do before its contract is admitted, give the core result values, and acquire the deciding owner sections for the task.\\n\\nPurpose: The owning sections for the method's canonical statement; the product lineage objects; the product definition's required relations, recursive discovery and the one constitutional surface with its staleness binding; the authority kinds, the frame tuple and the activation packet; the step's intake and admission; context construction with the size measurement, acquisition, activation and evaluation; and the core result algebra.\\n\\nBinds:\\n\\n- This task binds the construction relation: A is the exact subject and basis the activation binds, Z is the task's required outcome with the acceptance conditions the task states, and the actor's claims keep preservation, progress and outcome satisfaction distinct; a judgment its evidence cannot decide is `indeterminate`, and work it cannot finish is reported as unresolved work, not as a judgment ([../ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation](../ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation); member sha256=56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d; section sha256=6b6c2ce91c5a7e4be765af2f8009252fa8918719e1d885af6b5810ba4eb699da)\\n\\nA `Binds:` item names an obligation the activation of this frame binds, with\\na link to the owning section, the digest of its member and the digest of that\\nsection, or of the span of sections it names, where it names one; the item\\ncopies no section and owns no determination, and where no route of this frame\\ncarries the section the item is a paraphrase of it.\\n\\nEach excerpt below copies one owning section of a member of this method\\nbyte for byte, except a `rows=k/n` excerpt (see below) and except that\\neach relative link destination is rebased\\nto resolve from this directory to the same target. Fenced code, inline\\ncode and absolute and `stdo://` links are unchanged. The `Source:` line\\nbefore an excerpt names the member and the section's anchor, and gives\\nthe SHA-256 of the whole owning member. The section digest recorded in\\nFRAME_INPUTS.json is over the owner's bytes, not over this copy. The\\nowning section decides; this frame owns no determination. An excerpt\\nwhose `Source:` line says `rows=k/n` is a family table of which only\\nthe k rows that cite a section this frame carries are copied, with the\\ntable's preamble, header and every non-family table; the other rows\\nstay in the owning member and are not copied. The frame's\\nqualification, not this selection, decides whether the frame is\\nsufficient for its task.\\n\\nRoutes, in order:\\n\\n1. [SPEC_METHOD.md#canonical-statement](../SPEC_METHOD.md#canonical-statement)\\n2. [FOUNDATIONS.md#product-lineage-objects](../FOUNDATIONS.md#product-lineage-objects)\\n3. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#2-required-definition-relations](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#2-required-definition-relations)\\n4. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#9-recursive-discovery-and-explicit-composition](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#9-recursive-discovery-and-explicit-composition)\\n5. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#11-one-constitutional-surface-and-version-boundary](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#11-one-constitutional-surface-and-version-boundary)\\n6. [FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds](../FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)\\n7. [FOUNDATIONS.md#the-frame-tuple](../FOUNDATIONS.md#the-frame-tuple)\\n8. [REFERENCE_FRAME.md#11-the-activation-packet](../REFERENCE_FRAME.md#11-the-activation-packet)\\n9. [ACTIVATION.md#intake](../ACTIVATION.md#intake)\\n10. [ACTIVATION.md#admission](../ACTIVATION.md#admission)\\n11. [ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope](../ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope)\\n12. [FOUNDATIONS.md#results](../FOUNDATIONS.md#results)\\n13. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#foundation-to-law-binding-a-project-to-the-method](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#foundation-to-law-binding-a-project-to-the-method)\\n14. [REFERENCE_FRAME.md#foundation-to-law](../REFERENCE_FRAME.md#foundation-to-law)\\n15. [SPEC_METHOD.md#foundation-to-law-chain-outcome-and-build-tenant-binding](../SPEC_METHOD.md#foundation-to-law-chain-outcome-and-build-tenant-binding)\\n\\nSize of this frame: 84475 bytes.\\n\\nSource: SPEC_METHOD.md#canonical-statement sha256=b2773dc0c9feb429b6b357bcfd60e7df46e54db8adcb04dc8d6dbfa023b73677\\n\\n### Canonical statement\\n\\nThe method in one statement, each clause owned by a section of this corpus\\n. Specification is constitutional source, not\\ncommentary on code. The method defines the process constitution; intent,\\nproduct definition and requirements define the project constitution (§1).\\nSpecification defines WHAT; design and realisation define HOW (§2). Every\\nproduct under this method publishes a layout-neutral definition that locates\\nits governing constitution, local constitutional decisions, collective\\nreference-frame bases, WHAT, independent build-tenant HOW realisations, work\\nsurfaces and explicit product composition; the definition is a routing\\noverlay, not a rival truth surface\\n([PRODUCT_DEFINITION §1](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#1-overlay-and-layout-independence)). A material term\\nresolves only under its bounded-context identity, owning authority, selected\\nbasis and governed scope; equal spelling creates no cross-context meaning or\\nauthority; explicit imports, translations, equivalences and disambiguations\\ngovern those seams, and zero or multiple applicable meanings fail closed\\n([PRODUCT_DEFINITION §5](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#5-bounded-context-semantic-resolution)). Requirements define the full constitutional what:\\ncapabilities, guarantees, governance and verification obligations; design\\ndefines the structural how, and ADRs are one durable form of that record\\n(§2, §10). The lifecycle is a governed disambiguation pipeline: each major\\nboundary reduces the space of lawful interpretations and surfaces major\\nambiguity explicitly; detection is mandatory; blocking or escalation is\\npolicy under declared risk appetite, except for hard-stop prerequisite\\nfailures (§5; ACTIVATION §4). Products, applications, modules, functions,\\nbuild tenants and runtime surfaces are implementations of the constitutional\\ndocuments, not substitutes for them. Scenarios verify operational meaning\\nwhere capability claims need end-to-end proof ([ASSURANCE §4](../ASSURANCE.md#4-scenario-bundle)). Code realises\\ndecisions. Design is derivable from requirements, which are derivable from\\ngoals, intent and product definition; code is derivable from requirements\\nand design (§2). Iteration is cumulative repricing, not waterfall. Events,\\nprojection and delta reveal drift. Every live requirement family has design\\nownership, explicit classification and downstream closure or explicit\\ndeferment; every design record grounds itself in requirements; shipping\\nbehaviour traces back to constitutional authority (§2). Live constitutional\\nsurfaces are versioned history that change by supersession or withdrawal,\\nnever by silent in-place mutation (§2). New intent emerges from real use\\ncases hitting the current model through explicit gap analysis, not from ad\\nhoc pressure (§2). Sprints are execution-control batches for pricing proof\\ncost and forcing close review; they are not authority layers and cannot hide\\ndrift (§4).\\n\\n\\nSource: FOUNDATIONS.md#product-lineage-objects sha256=92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\\n\\n### Product lineage objects\\n\\nSoftware is recursive and compositional: a released product may build the\\nnext released version of itself, a dependent product, or downstream project\\nartifacts. Most taxonomy drift in recursive systems comes from collapsing\\nthe roles below into one overloaded word such as \\\"product\\\". Each role is an\\nobject with its own identity (P3). This member owns the bounded context\\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:recursive-product-taxonomy` and the concept\\nidentities below under the selected complete basis.\\n\\n| Term | Definition | Requires |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Substrate (`urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:substrate`) | a lower product or runtime used to build other products | P3 |\\n| Development product (`urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:development-product`) | the role of one exact install of a released product while that install acts as builder substrate for a source project; the role creates no new product identity and transfers no meaning or authority from the builder to the product being authored | P3, P6 |\\n| Source project (`urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:source-project`) | the mutable workspace building the next release cut | P3 |\\n| Release cut (`urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:release-cut`) | one immutable annotated release-candidate boundary over a published feature set | P3 |\\n| Product (`urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:product`) | the released immutable thing resulting when that release cut is accepted | P3 |\\n| Install (`urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:install`) | a stamped workspace instance of that released product | P3 |\\n| Artifact (`urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:artifact`) | any published output built by a source project or by a configured installed product | P3 |\\n| Product definition (`urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:product-definition`) | the present-tense source-project authority surface, conventionally carried by `PRODUCT.md`; it defines the current product WHAT for decomposition and is not the released product artifact | P3, P2 |\\n\\nThe governing rules: a mutable source workspace is not called a product;\\nwhen a released product acts as builder substrate, the exact install is\\nbound as a development product without confusing it with the product being\\nauthored; an immutable release cut or installed product is not confused\\nwith the mutable source project building the next cut; the product\\ndefinition is the surface of a source project, not the released product\\nartifact; products may depend on other products; installed products may\\nbuild the next version of themselves or other products. The compiler\\nanalogy is the intended model: bootstrap source, release P0, install P0,\\nuse P0 to build the source for P1, release P1. The taxonomy is load-bearing:\\nblurred, dependency and self-hosting errors compound quickly and are\\nexpensive to unwind. SPEC_METHOD §6 applies these objects to lineage and\\nrelease.\\n\\nRelease objects. A release cut has three neighbours that release keeps\\ndistinct from it and from each other (P3, P6).\\nA candidate source is the mutable source-project state constructing a\\npossible successor; it is non-operative for released consumers. A release\\nsubject is the exact declared product member set or artifact that one\\nrelease cut binds, described by that cut's release-scoped claims; a\\ncarrier that holds it does not thereby make co-located material a\\nmember. A version-line selector is a mutable\\nalias naming the highest-ordinal published release cut on one version\\nline of one project; it is convenient discovery, not immutable identity,\\nand not sufficient as an exact basis ([RELEASE §1](../RELEASE.md#1-context-and-position)\\nstates which).\\nEqual version text does not collapse these objects. A selector or a\\nmutable carrier may move; a release cut never moves. RELEASE §2 realises\\nthem, with the carriers that hold them, as refs of one release source.\\n\\n\\nSource: PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#2-required-definition-relations sha256=95afb85e4cf8f248a6f430be34ef288add61445dc43d9c8121239409b9fac231\\n\\n## 2. Required definition relations\\n\\nEach definition contains (P3, P6):\\n\\n- `product`: the stable product-definition identity, display name,\\n  source-project locator and an explicit bounded-context declaration or\\n  `null`;\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,160]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"cbf4a10e8d0b4ca2ab4a1f3ee28a85ffedc3298a0fba666949d9b091e82cc714\",\"selected_sha256\":\"514fbd77a5eda5a571268dc89e301b0b2535a89332ce9ca7ee2d49e93b4e4236\",\"size_bytes\":11815,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/frames/bootstrap.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,160]},\"sha256\":\"cbf4a10e8d0b4ca2ab4a1f3ee28a85ffedc3298a0fba666949d9b091e82cc714\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-lifecycle-m2ap70vo/codex/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 a4fd7326ebd923db0523e22b8ca2fd82bcb80fed2e0d870c83407d69c94da7cf --principal host call --request - <<'STDO_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"diagnostics-source-method-2-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1002,1055]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nSTDO_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:e1a2a69b139e97a0402771e5dc40d827a8e43688f141b9d45201c13f9de45ff2\",\"sha256\":\"e1a2a69b139e97a0402771e5dc40d827a8e43688f141b9d45201c13f9de45ff2\"},\"id\":\"diagnostics-source-method-2-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f3fec7f25044d6c85ddca1b572c435e82b81e142e0c075a83d5ea236498eb0b8]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Construction availability\\n\\nA step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\\nexists (P5, P6):\\n\\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\\n\\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\\n\\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\\n\\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \\\"a candidate is available\\\", never\\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\\n(P5, P6).\\n\\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\\n(P6).\\n\\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\\nP3).\\n\\n### Disposition\\n\\nThe decision owner disposes an assessed candidate with one of four\\nsemantic dispositions (§1, Roles and delegation; P6, P5). An assessor may recommend one; the\\nrecommendation is evidence for the decision owner, never a disposition\\n([EVALUATION §4](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results)). The disposition is the\\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1002,1055]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"341bd47613f7675227bcb87d393289927926f52b4b51a253207a06ab415c8881\",\"size_bytes\":3287,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1002,1055]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
